=2 Walkthrough
* You will have to reach the bottom of {z:Ra'Kaznar Turris} and examine the **Ominous Postern** for a long cutscene to complete the Mission. If you have access to {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court} Home Point #1, you can use that teleport and completely disregard the below, using the **Vertical Transit Device** to head into {z:Ra'Kaznar Turris}.
** After the cutscene finishes you will be in {z:Kamihr Drifts} at the (F-8) entrance to {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar}
* To reach {z:Ra'Kaznar Turris}, you'll have to head to {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court} first. To get there, you will be going through crystal structures and some Gates-type zone.

=2 Seven Routes
There are many routes you may choose - if you're paying attention to the story, each {p:Naakual} is guarding an entrance into the Serpentine Labyrinth.
Here they all are **from shortest to longest**[1] - remember that you only need to take one:
+ if you've cleared {p:Yumcax} (have {k:Aged Ligneous Naakual crest}), via {z:Yorcia Weald} through {z:Cirdas Caverns} **Map 2**.
++ This will put you very close to the {p:Home Point} on Map 2 when you arrive.
++ Can be painful to clear for new players due to {p:doom|Doom}.
++ See #Yorcia Weald below for a detailed guide.
+ if you've cleared {p:Tchakka} (have {k:Aged Riptide Naakual crest}), via {z:Foret de Hennetiel} through {z:Dho Gates} **Map 2**.
++ This Naakual is much easier to clear and it puts you significantly far into the trek.
+ if you've cleared {p:Hurkan} (have {k:Aged Booming Naakual crest}), via {z:Marjami Ravine} through {z:Woh Gates} **Map 2**.
++ See #Marjami Ravine below for a detailed guide.
+ if you've cleared {p:Achuka} (have {k:Aged Firebrand Naakual crest}), via {z:Morimar Basalt Fields} through {z:Moh Gates} **Map 2**.
+ if you've cleared {p:Colkhab} (have {k:Aged Matriarch Naakual crest}), via {z:Ceizak Battlegrounds} through {z:Sih Gates} **Map 2**. This is the last of the options that put you directly into {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court}.
+ if you've cleared {m:Kumhau} (have {k:Aged Flashfrost Naakual crest}), the gate at (D-8) of {z:Woh Gates} (Map 1, unlike the others!) will now be traversable, which will take you to __{z:Outer|Outer Ra'Kaznar}__ Map 2 at (L-8), where you can head to the elevator into {z:Inner|Ra'Kaznar Inner Court} at (I-8).
+ if you've cleared none of them, you need to do the full traversal from the start of {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar} (where the {p:Augural Conveyor} is and the exit to {z:Kamihr Drifts}).
++ See #Last Route below for a detailed guide.

=3 Yorcia Weald
\**{c=red:Note:}** This route may only be taken if you have cleared the {p:Wildskeeper Reive} for {z:Yorcia Weald} and thus have the {@k} {k:Aged Ligneous Naakual crest} Key Item.
* The shortest path starts at {z:Yorcia Weald} (I-11).
** Head to the **Enigmatic Device** (Alluvion Skirmish entrance) or **Waypoint 2** and head south to the crystal structure **???** (I-11) and warp to {z:Cirdas Caverns} (Map 2).
** Head north and examine the crystal structure at (H-6) to be warped to {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court} (Map 2).

=3 Marjami Ravine
\**{c=red:Note:}** This route may only be taken if you have cleared the {p:Wildskeeper Reive} for {z:Marjami Ravine} and thus have the {@k} {k:Aged Booming Naakual crest} Key Item.
* You may have to break a Colonization Reive in {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court} (Map 1).
* This route starts at {z:Marjami Ravine} (F-11).
** Proceed to Waypoint 3 and head east the crystal structure **???** to warp to {z:Woh Gates} (Map 2).
*** Head south east and climb down the **Scalable Area**.
*** Hug the right wall towards {m:Lapiniontraps|Lapiniontrap} and {m:Lapinions|Lapinion} around (E-12), yes it is odd they coexist.
*** On your left will be another **Scalable Area**, climb up it and examine the crystal structure **???** to be warped to {z:Woh Gates}.
** At (H-9) in {z:Woh Gates}, warp to {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court}.
** From (D-7) on Map 1, head southeast to (L-10/11), and you will be warped to (L/M-12) on Map 2.
*** Head southwest then north to (K-10). You may have to break a Colonization Reive here.
*** Head north to (K-8), and you will be at the same place as if you had taken the {z:Yorcia Weald} Route.
* Follow the left wall and use the **Vertical Transit Device** to enter {z:Ra'Kaznar Turris}.
* There is a {p:Home Point} next to the entrance (yay!).
* Head to the bottom and examine the **Ominous Postern** for a very long cutscene.

=3 Last Route
\**{c=red:Note:}** If you do not have either of the above {p:Naakual} crests for their respective zone. Then you'll have to take the "long" (trying to obtain the {p:Naakual} crests without a group can and will take longer than choosing this path) route, traversing all of {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar} and {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court}.
* You will have to pass through 2 Colonization Reives in {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar}, and 2 Colonization Reives in {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court} to get to {z:Ra'Kaznar Turris}.
** This requires {@k} {k:"Demolishing"}.
** You will need a {@k} {k:Silvery plate}, obtained within {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar} from the **???** at (C-7) (Map 1) in order to access {z:Ra'Kaznar Turris} via this route if you did not already obtain it earlier.
* Follow the arrows on the {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar} maps to the right. You must reach the eastern side of the central Elevator, on Map 2, (I-8).
** The starting point is either through {z:Kamihr Drifts} or more conveniently the **Enigmatic Warp** to the {p:Augural Conveyor} via an {p:Adoulin} {p:Waypoint}.
* Upon completing your run through {z:Outer Ra'Kaznar}, you will arrive at the {z:Inner Court|Ra'Kaznar Inner Court}, Map 1 (I-7).
* Using the marked map connections for {z:Ra'Kaznar Inner Court}, proceed to Warp **A** on Map 1 to reach **A** on Map 2.
** Then to **D** on Map 2, sending you to **D** Map 1.
** From **D** on Map 1 proceed to **H**.
** From **H** on Map 2 to **I**.
** From **I** on Map 1 to **J**.
* Finally, after using the **J** warp you will be right around the corner from the {p:Home Point} and zone. Good job surviving this nightmare.
* Head to the bottom and examine the **Ominous Postern** for a very long cutscene. (Down through the door by the {p:Home Point}, then further down, as down as you can go.)

